# module Chat handler boundary

Owns the complete Chat route after routing: body parsing, normalization, parameter
reporting, conversation selection, caller-tool suspension/resumption, ACP turn
execution, response shaping and release. Shared sink/session accounting primitives
come from `turn-runtime.js`; timer/disconnect ownership comes from
`turn-lifecycle.js`. `server.js` must not duplicate this handler.

# invariant Refuse before state

Malformed or unsupported parameters and unknown models must fail before a
conversation claim, tool bench, session admission or agent spawn.

# invariant Chat resumes the session that was opened

Every new Chat conversation stores `session.resumeContext`, including cwd, the
complete MCP declaration and the reasoning baseline. Parking returns that exact
context through key/prefix matching and resume uses it unchanged. A temporary
reasoning override must never become the baseline of the restored session.
